nt information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Sentence Stress", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class =\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\".", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Word stress is emphasis on <span class =\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class =\"strong\">word</span>.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class =\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class =\"strong\">sentence</span>.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Content words </span><ul>  \t<li>Content words are the important or key words of a sentence.<br /> They provide the meaning of the sentence.</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Structure words </span><ul>  \t<li>Structure words are not important words.<br /> They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct.</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Placing the stress on the wrong syllable in a word or placing stress on the wrong word in a sentence may lead to confusion or loss of meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "No \u2026 is she <span class=\"strong\">da</span> tingsomeone?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Haven't you<span class=\"strong\"> heard</span> about her co-worker<span class=\"strong\"> Mar</span>co?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well she<span class=\"strong\"> falls</span> for<span class=\"strong\"> guys</span> so<span class=\"strong\"> eas</span>ily.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I can<span class=\"strong\"> never</span> meet<span class=\"strong\"> any</span>one around here I would<span class=\"strong\"> ac</span>tually want to <span class=\"strong\">date</span>.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hunk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an attractive man ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa thinks that Marco is a hunk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about relationships.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to drool ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show admiration or desire for something or someone in an exaggerated way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was drooling over him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "well-traveled ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who has traveled a lot", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco is very well-traveled.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "naive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having or showing a lack of experience or knowledge ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa is so naive when it comes to guys.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "charmer ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who can convince others of their skills and abilities ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco is such a charmer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "love them and leave them ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not staying in a relationship for a long time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco is a love them and leave them kind of guy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "a lot in common ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have similar interests ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They might have a lot in common.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Say the words in the table below aloud.  Remember: Do <span class=\"strong\">not</span> add the short <span class=\"italic\">e</span> sound to the beginning of the word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Imagine you are inviting some of your friends over for a barbecue. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write an 8-10 line dialogue using at least six of these words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the dialogue aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"school\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Spain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"summer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Saturday\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"September\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sauce\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sausage\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sunday\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sunshine\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"slim\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shiny\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"salad\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I say and use words that start with the <span class=\"italic\">s</span> sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the dialogue aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le06ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le06ob04re2img06.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob04re2img06.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hi, Pete.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hey, what's up?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Not much. Did you hear about Vanessa's Aussie hunk?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hunk? No ... is she dating someone?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Haven't you heard about her co-worker Marco? She's drooling all over him. Marco's so clever, well-traveled and so good-looking ... blah ... blah ... blah ... blah."}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob04re2img07.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "23000", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: You sound a little jealous.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: No, I'm not. I think Vanessa is a little naive sometimes.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Naive? <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, she falls for guys so easily.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Maybe they just have a lot in common."}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob04re2img07.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "38000", "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: He sounds more like a charmer ... a love them and leave them kind of guy.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Don't worry, you won't be single for long.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I can never meet anyone around here I would actually want to date.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hmmm ... Some guys have all the luck."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le06ob04re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can pronounce words starting with the letter s. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can describe people's appearance and personality. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify key information in a short audio.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you like to know about other people's lives? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you like to gossip?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Pronunciation Spot: Have you heard the gossip? What is happening between Marco and Vanessa?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Sally and Peter <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">gossip</span> about Vanessa's new <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_1\">Aussie</span> love interest.  How does Sally feel?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "",